{# goal: Emit the Phase 0 condensation-triage output shapes for the doc-update skill: the triage table (CORE / FOLD / DELETE with named successors), the fold plan, and the lifecycle-ledger entry appended to kask/docs/README.md. Every decision needs a successor; "none" is only valid for DELETE rows whose content is fully obsolete. Feeds the <75-document cap check (working target 60). The Phase 6 gate results are reported by the skill's own convergence form, not by this template — gate data does not exist at Phase 0 render time. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    date: string
    count_before: number
    count_after: number
    reason_category: string
    triage_rows: array
    fold_rows: array
    ledger_rows: array
  output:
    triage_table: string
    fold_plan: string
    ledger_entry: string
---
## Condensation triage — {{ date }}

Tree count before: {{ count_before }} (cap: < 75, working target 60)
Tree count after (projected): {{ count_after }}

| Path | Role (CORE / FOLD / DELETE) | Reason | Successor |
|------|------------------------------|--------|-----------|
{%- for row in triage_rows %}
| {{ row.path }} | {{ row.role }} | {{ row.reason }} | {{ row.successor_or_none }} |
{%- endfor %}

## Fold plan (FOLD rows only)

For each FOLD: name the target section in the successor doc, the content
being carried forward, and the links that must be repointed.

| Source | Successor section | Content carried | Links to repoint |
|--------|-------------------|-----------------|------------------|
{%- for row in fold_rows %}
| {{ row.source }} | {{ row.section }} | {{ row.content }} | {{ row.links }} |
{%- endfor %}

## Lifecycle ledger entry (append to kask/docs/README.md)

### Deleted {{ date }} ({{ reason_category }})

| Artifact | Successor |
|----------|-----------|
{%- for row in ledger_rows %}
| {{ row.artifact }} | {{ row.successor }} |
{%- endfor %}

## Output

Respond with a JSON object:

```json
{
  "triage_table": "<the filled triage table>",
  "fold_plan": "<the filled fold plan>",
  "ledger_entry": "<the filled lifecycle-ledger entry>"
}
```
